  "limitations": [
    "Replay of DeepSeek observed timing and token counts under normalized Claude-like prices, not actual Claude behavior or invoice.",
    "Deterministic idealized rolling TTL with all prompt tokens written, append prefix proxy, reset at session/day/route/mutation/invalid/declining token counts. No backend hit guarantee, cross-session cache, exact cache key, write eligibility or breakpoint semantics. End-clock vs start-clock and prior-hit proxy sensitivity.",
    "Credit hypothetical covers modeled short-TTL rewrite increment only in 5–60m gaps, not actual Anthropic fallback credit. Credit leaves cache reconstruction unchanged.",
    "Same aggregate customer concessions do not imply same provider cost or welfare. Long TTL premium paid on modeled writes including first and final; no live storage cost.",
    "Week-local session-day groups, not unique customers. 200k cap sensitivity based on group maximum. Fixed discount rate computed on development, applied unchanged to final week."
